sequenceDiagram
    participant Caller
    participant fetchFn as fetch(name, type)
    participant createFn as create(parent, type, name, userId)
    participant DB as entity_entry (real, low-level)

    Caller->>fetchFn: fetch('Businesses', typeRootName)
    fetchFn->>DB: does 'Businesses' really exist?
    DB-->>fetchFn: yes, real entity found
    fetchFn-->>Caller: TypedNode of RootName

    Caller->>createFn: create(businessesNode, typeBusinessName, 'Acme', userId)
    createFn->>createFn: scoped uniqueness check (same rule as createEntity)
    createFn->>DB: INSERT INTO entity_entry
    DB-->>createFn: real, new entity_id allocated
    createFn-->>Caller: TypedNode of BusinessName

    Note over Caller,DB: A TypedNode of ProviderName can never be passed where a TypedNode of DivisionName parent is expected - a compile error, not a runtime check.
